# Infrastructure layer rules

- Infrastructure is the adapter layer for external systems (tokens, storage, queues, third-party providers).
- It implements Application contracts; it must not reshape the Domain model.
- Do not hard-code environment-specific settings (env/config/secrets); read them from configuration.
- Centralize resilience policies (retry, timeout, circuit breaker) here.
- Logging and observability carry technical detail only; do not leak sensitive business data.
- Normalize external service exceptions at the layer boundary; do not bubble raw provider exceptions upward.
- **Errors:** Do not throw **`ArgumentNullException`** / **`ArgumentException`** for validation; use **`GuardExtensions`** with **`AzoxiaErrorCodes`** (and registered **`ErrorCode`** values when added for infrastructure-specific failures) so callers see **`AzoxiaException`**. **`OperationCanceledException`** from **`CancellationToken.ThrowIfCancellationRequested()`** remains acceptable for cooperative cancellation.
- Keep naming and layout aligned with the project-wide C# conventions.
